FMutate expressive controls for FRASIL 3.4.1 (MPL-2.0, Copyright (C) 2026 Styves Goupil; preserving upstream attribution).

Adds volatile per-channel MIDI pitch bend (0xEn, +-2 semitones, center 8192, endpoints 0/16383,
routed to tracks listening on each channel and panel keys via the active keyboard track's channel,
combined with the SMK-37 physical pitch wheel on LEAD) and per-note square-law MIDI polyphonic
aftertouch expression gain (0xAn, 127 unity, 0 silent) with per-voice smoothing, channel and
source-key isolation (panel keys and internal sequencers unaffected), release-tail preservation,
and new-note/retrigger/steal reset across DRONE, GLINT, BASS, and LEAD; CC120 and CC123 release
notes while preserving held pitch bend, and CC121 resets pitch bend and polyphonic expression
without releasing held notes. Channel pressure (0xDn), CC11 swell, and SMK-37 key pressure remain
unchanged. Neutral sound without MIDI polyphonic pressure or pitch bend is bit-identical to stock
and persisted scene/state/live layouts are untouched.

